{
  "title": "OEM Fleet – GPU Drill-Down",
  "uid": "redfish-oem-fleet",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 2,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {"from": "now-1h", "to": "now"},
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "vendor",
        "label": "OEM",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": "Prometheus",
        "query": "label_values(redfish_system_health, vendor)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "multi": true,
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "gpu",
        "label": "GPU Type",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": "Prometheus",
        "query": "label_values(redfish_system_health{vendor=~\"$vendor\"}, gpu)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "multi": true,
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Server Count",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 4, "x": 0, "y": 0},
      "description": "Counted from up{job=\"redfish\"} (one series per configured target, filtered by vendor/gpu), not redfish_system_health: that metric is missing entirely for down targets and reports 2 series per host on HGX-baseboard hosts (the host system and the GPU baseboard), so counting it directly both undercounts down hosts and double-counts HGX hosts.",
      "targets": [{"expr": "count(up{job=\"redfish\", vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"})", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Servers"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "blue", "value": null}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "title": "Hosts Down",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 4, "x": 4, "y": 0},
      "description": "count(up{job=\"redfish\"} == 0) — pairs with Server Count and explains any gap in Total GPUs below (a down host's redfish_gpu_count_configured drops out entirely until its next successful scrape, see that panel's description). Backs the RedfishTargetDown alert (fires per-host after 10m down); this is the live, un-debounced count.",
      "targets": [{"expr": "count(up{job=\"redfish\", vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"} == 0) or vector(0)", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Down"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "red", "value": 1}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Total GPUs",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "Summed from inventory's gpu_count (redfish_gpu_count_configured), not counted from GPU temperature sensors: sensor granularity varies by vendor (e.g. this SuperMicro fleet exposes only 3 zone-level GPU temp sensors per 8-GPU host, not one per GPU), so counting sensor series undercounts real GPUs on those hosts. Only reflects currently-reachable hosts — see Hosts Down for what's currently excluded from this total.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 4, "x": 8, "y": 0},
      "targets": [{"expr": "sum(redfish_gpu_count_configured{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"}) or vector(0)", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "GPUs"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "blue", "value": null}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "GPUs Above 80°C",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 4, "x": 12, "y": 0},
      "targets": [{"expr": "count(redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"} > 80) or vector(0)", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Over Threshold"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "red", "value": 1}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "title": "GPUs Hot While Idle",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 4, "x": 16, "y": 0},
      "description": "Live count of the GPUHotWhileIdle condition (>45°C while the host trails its peer cohort's power draw — see prometheus/alert_rules.yml). This is the instantaneous count, not gated by the alert's 15m 'for' duration, so it can be non-zero here briefly before (or without) actually paging — check the GPU Hot While Idle section below for detail.",
      "targets": [{"expr": "count((redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"} > 45) and on (instance) (redfish_power_watts{name=~\"System Power Control|Server Power Control\"} < on (vendor, gpu_count) group_left quantile(0.15, redfish_power_watts{name=~\"System Power Control|Server Power Control\"}) by (vendor, gpu_count))) or vector(0)", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Idle+Hot"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "red", "value": 1}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "title": "Active Critical Alerts",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 4, "x": 20, "y": 0},
      "description": "count(ALERTS{alertstate=\"firing\", severity=\"critical\"}) — ServerHealthCritical, GPUFailure, PowerSupplyFailure, DiskFailure. Unlike the other tiles in this row (which read the raw metric right now), this only counts alerts that have already cleared their 'for' duration in prometheus/alert_rules.yml, i.e. confirmed, sustained problems Alertmanager has actually paged on.",
      "targets": [{"expr": "count(ALERTS{alertstate=\"firing\", severity=\"critical\", vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"}) or vector(0)", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Critical"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "red", "value": 1}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "title": "GPU Hot While Idle",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 4}
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "title": "GPUs Hot Without Matching Load (°C)",
      "description": "Same condition as the GPUHotWhileIdle alert, same style as the Top 10 Hottest GPUs bar below: GPU sensor above 45°C while the host's total power draw trails well behind its same-vendor/GPU-count peers right now (bottom 15th percentile of the live cohort — see prometheus/alert_rules.yml for why this is peer-relative rather than a fleet-wide watt cutoff or each host's own history). Placed ahead of Top 10 Hottest because a hot-but-idle GPU is a stronger signal of a real problem (stuck process, stuck P-state, tray cooling fault) than a hot GPU that's simply under real load.",
      "type": "bargauge",
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 5},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(10, (redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"} > 45) and on (instance) (redfish_power_watts{name=~\"System Power Control|Server Power Control\"} < on (vendor, gpu_count) group_left quantile(0.15, redfish_power_watts{name=~\"System Power Control|Server Power Control\"}) by (vendor, gpu_count)))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} · {{name}} [{{vendor}}/{{gpu}}]"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 45}, {"color": "red", "value": 55}]},
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Open Server Detail",
              "url": "/d/redfish-server-detail/server-detail?var-instance=${__field.labels.instance}&var-vendor=${__field.labels.vendor}&var-gpu=${__field.labels.gpu}",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "title": "GPUs Hot Without Matching Load",
      "description": "Same condition as the GPUHotWhileIdle alert: GPU sensor above 45°C while the host's total power draw trails well behind its same-vendor/GPU-count peers right now (bottom 15th percentile of the live cohort — see prometheus/alert_rules.yml for why this is peer-relative rather than a fleet-wide watt cutoff or each host's own history). redfish_power_watts is chassis-total, not per-GPU, so on multi-sensor hosts (Dell/HGX) compare the flagged sensor against its siblings in this table to see if it's an isolated GPU or the whole zone — that distinction matters for triage (single stuck process vs. a tray-level cooling fault). Confirmed twice already (10.20.32.147, 10.20.32.137) to catch real issues, not idle-baseline noise.",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 13},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "(redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"} > 45) and on (instance) (redfish_power_watts{name=~\"System Power Control|Server Power Control\"} < on (vendor, gpu_count) group_left quantile(0.15, redfish_power_watts{name=~\"System Power Control|Server Power Control\"}) by (vendor, gpu_count))",
          "instant": true,
          "format": "table",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "sortBy": [{"displayName": "Value", "desc": true}],
        "footer": {"show": false}
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Open Server Detail",
              "url": "/d/redfish-server-detail/server-detail?var-instance=${__data.fields.instance}&var-vendor=${__data.fields.vendor}&var-gpu=${__data.fields.gpu}",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "Value"},
            "properties": [
              {"id": "unit", "value": "celsius"},
              {"id": "custom.displayMode", "value": "color-background"},
              {"id": "thresholds", "value": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 45}, {"color": "red", "value": 55}]}}
            ]
          },
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "Time"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "__name__"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "job"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "exported_vendor"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Top 10 Hottest GPUs",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 21}
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Top 10 Hottest GPUs (°C)",
      "type": "bargauge",
      "gridPos": {"h": 12, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 22},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(10, redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"})",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} · {{name}} [{{vendor}}/{{gpu}}]"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 70}, {"color": "red", "value": 80}]},
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Open Server Detail",
              "url": "/d/redfish-server-detail/server-detail?var-instance=${__field.labels.instance}&var-vendor=${__field.labels.vendor}&var-gpu=${__field.labels.gpu}",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Fleet GPU Temperature Summary",
      "description": "Min / average / max across the fleet — the baseline context for the two anomaly lists above, and the more actionable question for cooling/placement than any single GPU outlier.",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 34}
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Max GPU Temp (Fleet)",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 35},
      "targets": [{"expr": "max(redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"})", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Max Temp"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 70}, {"color": "red", "value": 80}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Fleet Avg GPU Temp",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 8, "x": 8, "y": 35},
      "targets": [{"expr": "avg(redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"})", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Avg"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 70}, {"color": "red", "value": 80}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Coolest GPU",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 8, "x": 16, "y": 35},
      "targets": [{"expr": "min(redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"})", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "Min"}],
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}, "colorMode": "background"},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 70}, {"color": "red", "value": 80}]}
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Temperature Trend",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 39}
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Top 10 Hottest GPUs – Temperature Trend",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {"h": 10, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 40},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(10, redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} · {{name}} [{{vendor}}]"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi"},
        "legend": {"displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["last", "max"]}
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "custom": {"lineWidth": 2, "thresholdsStyle": {"mode": "line+area"}},
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 70}, {"color": "red", "value": 80}]},
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Open Server Detail",
              "url": "/d/redfish-server-detail/server-detail?var-instance=${__field.labels.instance}&var-vendor=${__field.labels.vendor}&var-gpu=${__field.labels.gpu}",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "GPU Health Overview",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 50}
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "GPU Status – All Servers (by Temperature)",
      "description": "This BMC firmware never reports GPUs as Processor/Accelerator resources, so redfish_gpu_health has no series to show — that metric is permanently empty here, not a query bug. This table shows real per-GPU status instead, derived from temperature against the same 70°C/80°C thresholds used fleet-wide.",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {"h": 10, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 51},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "redfish_gpu_temperature_celsius{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "format": "table",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "sortBy": [{"displayName": "Value", "desc": true}],
        "footer": {"show": false}
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Open Server Detail",
              "url": "/d/redfish-server-detail/server-detail?var-instance=${__data.fields.instance}",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "Value"},
            "properties": [
              {"id": "unit", "value": "celsius"},
              {"id": "custom.displayMode", "value": "color-background"},
              {"id": "thresholds", "value": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "yellow", "value": 70}, {"color": "red", "value": 80}]}}
            ]
          },
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "Time"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "__name__"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "job"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "exported_vendor"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Server Fleet Health",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 61}
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "Server Health – All Servers",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {"h": 10, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 62},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "redfish_system_health{vendor=~\"$vendor\", gpu=~\"$gpu\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "format": "table",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "sortBy": [{"displayName": "Value", "desc": false}],
        "footer": {"show": false}
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Open Server Detail",
              "url": "/d/redfish-server-detail/server-detail?var-instance=${__data.fields.instance}",
              "targetBlank": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "Value"},
            "properties": [
              {"id": "mappings", "value": [{"type": "value", "options": {"0": {"text": "CRITICAL", "color": "red", "index": 0}, "0.5": {"text": "WARNING", "color": "yellow", "index": 1}, "1": {"text": "OK", "color": "green", "index": 2}}}]},
              {"id": "custom.displayMode", "value": "color-background"}
            ]
          },
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "Time"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "__name__"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "job"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]},
          {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "exported_vendor"}, "properties": [{"id": "custom.hidden", "value": true}]}
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
